186065283 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065417 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065284 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065284 #edb/ref 1061 77825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065284 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "503ce197-02ae-5ae2-897a-80af7de15a2a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065284 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064358 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065285 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186065286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065285 #edb/ref 1061 77828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065285 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b129822d-f637-5611-9cad-e2f8b6aefca4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065285 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186065418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065286 #edb/ref 1061 77829 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065286 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8ddc832d-59f9-5fa2-85e2-002f7b9c4ccc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065286 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065416 #edb/ref 1064 "Dividing with negative numbers follows similar rules as multiplying with negative numbers. \n\nFirst of all, a negative number divided by a positive number gives a negative number. We can picture this rule as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-)\\,÷\\,(+)\\,=\\,(-).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example, let's use this rule to find the value of $(-6) \\div 2.$\n\nHere, since we are dividing a negative number $\\color{red}(-6)$ by a positive number ${\\color{blue}(2)},$ the result is going to be negative:\n![](images/b6/b64108fa03fc286ddcd04ac4cd7a9d77c1672d0ced66ebb1953c97afa5488533.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $6$ by $2$ *without* any signs: $6 \\div 2 = 3.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-6)} \\div {\\color{blue}2} = {\\color{red} -3 }.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065416 #edb/ref 1065 8108 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065416 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b92ac2e4-b983-5fd5-bc18-7dfb821497f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065416 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065417 #edb/ref 1064 "A positive number divided by a negative number is also a negative number. We can picture this rule as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(+)\\,÷\\,(-)\\,=\\,(-).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor instance, to find $8\\div (-2),$ we have to divide a positive number $\\color{blue}(8)$ by a negative one ${\\color{red}(-2)}.$ So the result will be negative:\n![](images/79/797eda7126fff569fccda2681c628f99f103057d7c5e23c1b65cb566b48ef203.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $8$ by $2$ without any signs: $8 \\div 2 = 4.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}8} \\div {\\color{red}(-2)} = {\\color{red}-4}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065417 #edb/ref 1065 8109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065417 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "67beb927-7da4-5576-8982-1a823c878691" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065417 #edb/ref 1067 "The Quotient of a Positive and a Negative is a Negative" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065418 #edb/ref 1064 "Finally, the third rule is that a negative number divided by a negative number is a positive number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-)\\,÷\\,(-)\\,=\\,(+)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo demonstrate, let's find $-12 \\div (-3).$ We have to divide a negative number $\\color{red}(-12)$ by another negative number ${\\color{red}(-3)}.$ So the result will be positive:\n![](images/d3/d31776de6ab95f8178d0bdd6e3b34cfa2f4fc0b987851dcace50aff1818936da.svg)\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $12$ by $3$ without any signs: $12 \\div 3 = 4.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-12)} \\div {\\color{red}(-3)} = {\\color{blue}4}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065418 #edb/ref 1065 8111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065418 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b1d3d95e-7953-5c5b-b97b-d4eb85e1f80d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065418 #edb/ref 1067 "The Quotient of a Negative and a Negative is a Positive" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490509 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186491239 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490509 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186491242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490509 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186491250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490509 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490509 #edb/ref 1045 "Dividing With Negative Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490509 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186491250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490509 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490509 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490509 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "c415186d-7a79-528f-ade9-bfd554821382" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490526 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490526 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490526 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "08c411ff-06f1-50ae-9d29-1123f1bab60d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490559 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490559 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490559 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "17caec73-9eb6-523a-86fb-b27f98488576" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490645 #edb/ref 1080 "22" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490645 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490645 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "47bce39b-7e6b-582c-8a7b-066f77808d00" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490683 #edb/ref 1080 "-4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490683 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490683 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5bc6dc80-cdb9-5185-ba72-5b0da18b7582" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490773 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490773 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490773 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8249b61b-93f1-54d1-854b-9e287db3d2d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490784 #edb/ref 1080 "-3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490784 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417